-- 126_help_articles_content_reconciliation.sql
-- RECONCILIATION -- this content is ALREADY LIVE. Captures help_articles
-- content for the two categories completed so far (Staff & Permissions 28,
-- Troubleshooting 16 = 44 rows), which were written to production by direct
-- SQL and never entered migration history.
--
-- Written as an idempotent UPSERT, not UPDATE-by-id, and this is deliberate:
-- 122_help_articles.sql creates the table but seeds ZERO rows, so the base
-- English content was never in migration history either. An UPDATE-only
-- reconciliation would silently affect 0 rows on a fresh environment and
-- would NOT meet the stated goal of "a fresh environment reproduces them."
-- This file carries the full row (EN + ES + keywords) so it actually does.
--
-- STILL OUTSTANDING (pre-existing gap, wider than today's changes): the
-- other 56 help_articles rows -- Getting Started 10, Inventory 9, Jewish
-- Calendar 14, Multi-Property 6, Recipes & Meals 10, Shopping 7 -- are also
-- absent from migration history and have no Spanish yet. They need the same
-- treatment as their translations land.
--
-- Generated programmatically from the live rows, not transcribed by hand:
-- these are staff-facing instructions in a language that cannot be eyeballed
-- for silent typos here, so machine generation + a hash check was the only
-- honest path.
--
-- FAQ-040's English correction is included in the values below: it had
-- directed staff to "My Day > Tasks > Household Instructions", a page that
-- has never existed. StaffOnboardingModal (messages/en.json:384) already
-- said the correct thing ("Check Shift Handover").

on conflict (id) do update set
  category = excluded.category,
  question = excluded.question,
  short_answer = excluded.short_answer,
  detailed_answer = excluded.detailed_answer,
  question_es = excluded.question_es,
  short_answer_es = excluded.short_answer_es,
  detailed_answer_es = excluded.detailed_answer_es,
  keywords = excluded.keywords;
